---
title: Mai Tai
servings: 1
tags: [cocktail, rum]
source: Our own
---

In a #cocktail shaker{}(with ice), pour @light rum{2%fl_oz} and @lime juice{1%fl_oz}(about a lime worth), @curacao{0.5%fl_oz}, @orgeat{0.25%fl_oz}, and @simple syrup{0.25%fl_oz}. Shake briskly for ~{10%seconds}, and strain into a #rocks glass{}(well chilled, with ice). Garnish with a @lime{1%wedge} and a @mint{1%sprig}.

> Trader Vic used Jamaican rum in the original. Can substitute Cointreau or Grand Marnier for curacao, if it is unavailable.
